{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>You were shown to know.</b> He says: You were shown signs and wonders, through which you can know that YHWH is the Elohim — there is none besides Him. And so immediately following: ״והשבות אל לבבך״." "<b>And open</b> the eyes of your understanding to this: for you will not find in all the Torah any expression anywhere saying ״האלהים הוא ה׳״, but only ״ה׳ הוא האלהים״; and so in the matter of Elijah (I Kings 18:39): ״ויפלו על פניהם ויאמרו ה׳ הוא האלהים״. For there are revealed miracles and there are hidden miracles, and the hidden are included within the revealed — and the discerning will understand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:31.584819157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}